.TH SESSLINT-HOOK 1 "" "SessLint 0.3.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-hook \- [read\-only] Agent hook entrypoint: reads one hook payload from stdin and checks the transcript.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint hook \-\-event NAME [\-\-json] [\-\-fail\-on {never,error,warning}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}]
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Reads one JSON hook payload from stdin (Claude Code contract: session_id, transcript_path, cwd, hook_event_name), resolves the transcript file, and runs the event\-appropriate integrity check. Prints one content\-free line and exits 0 (advisory) — or 1 when \-\-fail\-on gates on findings. Exit 2 is never emitted: hook checks never block the agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-event NAME
Hook event name (e.g. SessionStart, PreCompact, PostCompact, SessionEnd). Unknown names run the generic integrity check.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit sesslint.hook\-result/v1 JSON instead of the one\-line form
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on {never,error,warning}
Minimum finding severity that exits 1 (default: never — hook checks are advisory; 'warning' fails on any finding) Choices: never, error, warning.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Validation profile (default: neutral)
.TP
.B \-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}
Session format adapter (default: auto\-detect) Choices: auto, claude\-code\-jsonl, openai\-agents, codex\-rollout, canonical.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
